     * Sports and Off) sends nothing.
     *
     * A server that predates screen lists drops `SetScreens` silently, so
     * for one of those (known from this board's last BoardState) the call is
     * ROUTED to the legacy commands it does understand: `SetOffMode` naming
     * the first idle member's kind ("blank" when none is checked), then one
     * `SetOffModeParam` per per-screen value of that member. The single
     * ordered writer guarantees the mode lands before its params, which the
     * old server validates against the selected mode. Add, remove, reorder
     * and a second idle screen cannot be expressed that way; the platforms
     * hide them (`screens_editable`, `idle_single_select`).
     *
     * A board whose state has not arrived yet is sent NOTHING. Any list a
     * platform could build then started from the core's synthesized
     * default (the board's real list is unknown), so sending it — as
     * `SetScreens`, which a queued command does the moment the socket
     * re-auths, before the BoardState — would replace the board's real
     * screens, layouts and checkmarks with that default.
     *
     * The route is chosen when the call is made. An edit queued across a
     * server swap (a rollback to a server without lists while the socket
     * was down) goes out as `SetScreens`, which that server drops; the next
     * BoardState then shows the board as it really is.
     */
    func setScreens(boardId: String, screens: [UiScreenConfig])

    /**
     * Spoiler-protect every game on the board.
     */
    func setSpoilerAll(boardId: String, on: Bool)

    /**
     * How spoiler-protected games render: strict = matchup + time only.
     */
    func setSpoilerMode(boardId: String, strict: Bool)

    /**
     * Set a league's favourites and the rounds it subscribes to.
     *
     * `championship_option_ids` is the whole selection, sent as `Some` even
     * when empty — the server reads absent as "an older app that never knew
     * about rounds" and would expand the legacy field instead of deselecting.
     */
    func setSportConfig(boardId: String, sportId: String, favoriteTeamIds: [String], championshipOptionIds: [String])

    /**
     * Spoiler-protect one team's games.
     */
    func setTeamSpoiler(boardId: String, sportId: String, teamId: String, on: Bool)

    /**
     * Board-local IANA timezone ("America/New_York") — drives the board's
     * idle clock and start-time labels. Invalid names are ignored server-side.
     */
    func setTimezone(boardId: String, tz: String)

    /**
     * Remove a board AND revoke this app's pairing on the server. The grant
     * used to be permanent — re-adding the board later means pairing again
     * with a fresh code, which is what "Remove this scoreboard" implies.
     * Only this controller's own grant is revoked; other paired phones keep
     * theirs.
     */
    func unpairBoard(boardId: String)

    /**
     * Tell a board to download, verify, and install the server-hosted
     * firmware image (the one advertised via `on_board_version`'s
     * `update_available`). The board goes offline while it flashes and
     * reboots (~a minute); the fresh version report on reconnect is the
     * confirmation.
     */
    func updateFirmware(boardId: String)
}

